<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  RUT_ThrummelSeepwax_RosterSource.xml  UtinniPatches — SUMP_TAR_NASTINESS_1
                                         reconciliation

  RUT_ThrummelSeepwax (Defs/ThingDefs_Items/RUT_Tarred_Solvents.xml) shipped
  with no recipeMaker, "awaiting its real source, the hive raid" — the
  thrummel creature/hive did not exist yet. SUMP_FAUNA_ROSTER_1 has since
  shipped the thrummel family as real wildlife (RM_Thrummel/
  RM_ThrummelWarden/RM_ThrummelBroodmother, RM_TheSump), but their own
  butcherProducts award a SEPARATE RM-tier good, RM_Seepwax — RM tier may
  not depend on RUT tier (Q11a), so the free mod's own creatures could never
  drop this campaign-tier def directly. That roster item's own header named
  exactly this reconciliation as owed to "whoever next picks up
  SUMP_TAR_NASTINESS_1."

  The two goods are the same substance under two names, by design (compare
  descriptions: RUT_ThrummelSeepwax "warm, waxy secretion harvested from a
  thrummel mound"; RM_Seepwax "warm, waxy comb-secretion cracked from a
  thrummel mound... worked from tar-sugars by the workers") — so this is a
  cheap render step, not a refinement, matching that near-identity: 1:1,
  low WorkToMake (60, well under RUT_WeakTarSolvent's own 150 for an actual
  chemical conversion). Same PatchOperationConditional/PatchOperationSequence
  shape as RUT_Bitumen_KorvethSource.xml's own sibling reconciliation —
  RUT_Tarred_Solvents.xml itself is left untouched.

  This does not touch "the hive raid" as a source — RUT_ThrummelSeepwax
  remains tradeable/debug-spawnable with no live raid mechanic to attach to
  (SUMP_FAUNA_ROSTER_1's own deferred list: "thrummel mound + defend-radius
  comp... UNMEASURED, flagged for the Desktop") — it adds a second, real,
  working path via ordinary wildlife butchering, which the roster pass DID
  ship.
-->
<Patch>

  <Operation Class="PatchOperationConditional" MayRequire="mandrake.rm.thesump">
    <xpath>Defs/ThingDef[defName="RUT_ThrummelSeepwax"]</xpath>
    <match Class="PatchOperationSequence">
      <operations>
        <li Class="PatchOperationAdd">
          <xpath>Defs/ThingDef[defName="RUT_ThrummelSeepwax"]</xpath>
          <value>
            <recipeMaker>
              <recipeUsers>
                <li>TableMachining</li>
              </recipeUsers>
              <workSpeedStat>GeneralLaborSpeed</workSpeedStat>
              <workSkill>Crafting</workSkill>
              <displayPriority>415</displayPriority>
              <productCount>1</productCount>
            </recipeMaker>
            <costList>
              <RM_Seepwax>1</RM_Seepwax>
            </costList>
          </value>
        </li>
        <li Class="PatchOperationAdd">
          <xpath>Defs/ThingDef[defName="RUT_ThrummelSeepwax"]/statBases</xpath>
          <value>
            <WorkToMake>60</WorkToMake>
          </value>
        </li>
      </operations>
    </match>
  </Operation>

</Patch>
